I was looking for a dramatic "right time" to do this, but it
has been the "right time" for a long time, and it's likely to
continue to be, so I might as well say it now.

The NetHack 3.0 project with its fantastic public participation
would not have been possible without the dedicated offices, the
enthusiasm, and the patience of Bill Randle (billr@saab.cna.tek.com),
moderator of comp.sources.games.

Without the generous availability of the comp.sources.games platform,
we would have been forced to develop the game in private, posting only
the final results.  Bill Randle made it possible for the development
_process_ to be public (as much as such a process can be), and thus
he enabled an actual participation by you, the interested public, in the
code's development.  Your ability to look at the _stages_ of the 
development (the Patches) made your comments and criticisms effective
and crucially important in shaping the outcome.

Our heartfelt thanks to Bill Randle, and comp.sources.games.  The man
deserves applaud from the development team and the readership of 
rec.games.hack.  Let him hear it.

For the Development Team,

-Izchak


